@bank all
// Head writer 0607: clothes and laundry (the onboarding engineer's, plan-0607 "Clothes and laundry"). TEXTS, except
// clothes.remark (crew, a bubble or card line, gated on flag:clothes.stale: you're in yesterday's clothes after 10:00;
// gentle, never mean). {n} a count, {time} a clock time, plus the washer's number as {n} in laundry.busy.

== clothes.change
- Change clothes

== clothes.changed
- Fresh clothes. You feel ready for the day.
- Clean clothes on. Much better.

== clothes.left
- {n} clean outfits left.

== clothes.spare
- Your one spare outfit. The rest of your kit comes up from stores.

== clothes.stale
- You're in yesterday's clothes.

== clothes.empty
- No clean clothes left. Take the hamper to the laundry on Deck 4.

== clothes.hamper
- Take the hamper

== clothes.putaway
- Put the clothes away

== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Same shirt as yesterday? No judgement. Bit of judgement.   #funny
- Laundry's on Deck 4, if you're looking for it.
- Long night? You look like you slept in that.   #funny
- Hamper full? The washers are past the washrooms.
- I did that my first week too. The laundry's not scary.

== tip.laundry
- Out of clean clothes. Carry the hamper to the laundry on Deck 4, past the washrooms in the junior wing. Load a washer, and come back when it's done.

== laundry.load
- Load the washer

== laundry.running
- Washing. Done at {time}. You can leave it.

== laundry.busy
- All four washers are going. Number {n} finishes first, at {time}.

== laundry.done
- Your washing's done. Collect it from the laundry on Deck 4.

== laundry.collect
- Take out the washing

== laundry.fold
- Fold it first? Neat clothes, neat mind.

== laundry.away
- All put away. Five clean outfits.

== laundry.kit
- The rest of your kit has arrived from stores. Five outfits in your wardrobe now.

// Day 1 (playtest 1, O4): the clothes tip
== tip.clothes
- Fresh clothes are in your wardrobe: change each morning. When you run out, do your laundry on Deck 4.

// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: the green tip for dirty clothes, once for each state (AC3's clothesDirtyTick,
// worksText). Facts from section 21b: change at your wardrobe in Bunk 1; a change while grubby always takes a clean
// outfit; a shower leaves the grime; either state makes you feel grubby sooner (one CLOTHES_DRAIN).
== clothes.tip.yesterday
- You're in yesterday's clothes, and people notice. Change at your wardrobe in Bunk 1.
== clothes.tip.grubby
- Your uniform's grubby. A shower won't fix it: change at your wardrobe in Bunk 1.
== clothes.tip.yesterday2
// (FX4, 0.92.4 item B: the second green tip, a later day still in yesterday's clothes; ZW1 may reword)
- Yesterday's clothes again. A fresh set's waiting in your wardrobe in Bunk 1.
== clothes.tip.laundry
// (FX4, 0.92.4 item B, RV11: in yesterday's clothes with no clean ones left, either tip says this instead; ZW1 may reword)
- No clean clothes left. Take your hamper to the laundry on Deck 4.
